      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e A good way to break this up would be to add build support, then cpu detection, followed by individual optimizations split by file.\n\u003e \n\u003e Will do\n\u003e \n\u003e \u003e In other libraries, like libvpx, we disabled CI support for PPC some time ago and left it to others to handle testing and maintenance (there are bugs if you\u0027re interested).\n\u003e \n\u003e Yes, I am. I can also try to set up PPC64 GitHub Runner (sponsored by IBM) on my GitHub mirror repository.\n\nThat would be great.\n\nOn the libvpx side there are at least two open PPC related bugs:\n\n* https://issues.webmproject.org/42330687\n* https://issues.webmproject.org/42330554",
